\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textsc  {Lazy SF-FSA-VI} (Algorithm~\ref {alg:lazy}) with exact SFs, starting from the 6 extreme policies. (a) Maximum relative regret over the tasks of zero-shot SF-FSA-VI over the extreme policies and over the whole $\varepsilon $-CCS of SFOLS; Algorithm~\ref {alg:lazy} has zero regret on every task. (b) Policies stored by Algorithm~\ref {alg:lazy} when the added policies are kept over the sequence of tasks. (c) How the added policies were certified: as the metapolicy, as $\pi ^{\mathrm  {hyb}}$, or after policy iteration, starting from the extreme policies on every task or keeping the added ones (the number of added policies is on the right).}}{20}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:lazy}{{4}{20}{\textsc {Lazy SF-FSA-VI} (Algorithm~\ref {alg:lazy}) with exact SFs, starting from the 6 extreme policies. (a) Maximum relative regret over the tasks of zero-shot SF-FSA-VI over the extreme policies and over the whole $\varepsilon $-CCS of SFOLS; Algorithm~\ref {alg:lazy} has zero regret on every task. (b) Policies stored by Algorithm~\ref {alg:lazy} when the added policies are kept over the sequence of tasks. (c) How the added policies were certified: as the metapolicy, as $\pi ^{\mathrm {hyb}}$, or after policy iteration, starting from the extreme policies on every task or keeping the added ones (the number of added policies is on the right)}{figure.4}{}}
\abx@aux@cite{0}{kuric_planning_2024}
\abx@aux@segm{0}{0}{kuric_planning_2024}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textsc  {Lazy SF-FSA-VI} without a model, in the windy domain (60 tasks, top) and the Office domain with $p = 0.3$ (33 tasks, bottom), mean over 10 seeds. (a, c) A new task: relative regret of the executed plan against the environment steps spent on the task. \textsc  {Lazy SF-FSA-VI} starts from the 6 learned extreme policies and grows with the metapolicy or with Q-learning over all actions, Q-learning on the product MDP starts from scratch, and SF-FSA-VI over the policies of SFOLS spends nothing per task (horizontal line at its final regret). (b, d) Cumulative environment steps over the sequence of tasks, including the extreme policies, when the added policies are kept. The band is the range over seeds.}}{22}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:lazy_mf}{{5}{22}{\textsc {Lazy SF-FSA-VI} without a model, in the windy domain (60 tasks, top) and the Office domain with $p = 0.3$ (33 tasks, bottom), mean over 10 seeds. (a, c) A new task: relative regret of the executed plan against the environment steps spent on the task. \textsc {Lazy SF-FSA-VI} starts from the 6 learned extreme policies and grows with the metapolicy or with Q-learning over all actions, Q-learning on the product MDP starts from scratch, and SF-FSA-VI over the policies of SFOLS spends nothing per task (horizontal line at its final regret). (b, d) Cumulative environment steps over the sequence of tasks, including the extreme policies, when the added policies are kept. The band is the range over seeds}{figure.5}{}}
